{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The first time</b><br>רהיטנו. From the language of Mishnah: רהיטי ביתו של אדם (the beams of a man's house)." "ברותים. It has no parallel, and all the commentators said it is like ברושים (cypresses), except that [the letters] do not interchange except for אהו״י." "<b>The third time</b><br>He said: Knesset Israel — I desired (in the Tabernacle) to serve You [at] first, and afterward I will build You a house of cedars. (But) I am like a lily in the valley — (all who) pass by will trample it, and the fear that the Egyptians instilled in me is finished."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "Bracketed material appears in the Hebrew base text without explicit lemma marking; placed in brackets following the syntax of the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:57.303414963Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}